## Summary

Shipped a production-polished, Apple-idiomatic **`FeedbackModal`** SwiftUI surface at parity with `web/src/components/feedback/FeedbackModal.tsx`, following the established P4 modal architecture (mirroring predecessors `AddAnnotationPopover` 0002 / `ShareDriveDialog` 0028).

**11 files committed** (`apps/apple/TeslaSync/modals-dialogs/FeedbackModal.*`, 2,316 LOC) + gate log:
- **Pure core** (`.Adapter`, `.Seams`): category catalog, validation (zod min/max parity), context phase resolution, console-tail truncation, conditional-attach submission builder, telemetry/submit/source seams, i18n facade.
- **State holder** (`.Model`): `@MainActor @Observable`, async submit lifecycle, touched-gated validation, stale auto-refresh, `view.opened`.
- **Views** (`.swift`, `.Views`, `.Controls`, `.States`, `.Previews`): header + freshness chip + close, category `Picker`, Title/Details fields, the Auto-attached-context panel (Page/App version/Browser + 2 consent toggles) that phase-switches loading/empty/error, submit-error alert, Cancel/Send footer.

**Parity:** all states render (loading/empty/error/stale/offline/content + in-flight + submit-failure); the form always shows while the diagnostics panel switches phase (web parity). No web Tailwind ported — P1/S9 tokens via `TSGlassPanel`/`TSFadeIn`/`TSButton`.

